ta-track-load=3D"description_content"><p>Given the <code>root</code> of a b=
inary search tree, and an integer <code>k</code>, return <em>the</em> <code=
>k<sup>th</sup></code> <em>smallest value (<strong>1-indexed</strong>) of a=
ll the values of the nodes in the tree</em>.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>
<img alt=3D"" src=3D"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/01/28/kthtree=
1.jpg" style=3D"width: 212px; height: 301px;">
<pre><strong>Input:</strong> root =3D [3,1,4,null,2], k =3D 1
<strong>Output:</strong> 1
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>
<img alt=3D"" src=3D"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/01/28/kthtree=
2.jpg" style=3D"width: 382px; height: 302px;">
<pre><strong>Input:</strong> root =3D [5,3,6,2,4,null,null,1], k =3D 3
<strong>Output:</strong> 3
</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li>The number of nodes in the tree is <code>n</code>.</li>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D k &lt;=3D n &lt;=3D 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>
	<li><code>0 &lt;=3D Node.val &lt;=3D 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>
</ul>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Follow up:</strong> If the BST is modified often (i.e., we can d=
o insert and delete operations) and you need to find the kth smallest frequ=
ently, how would you optimize?</p>
